# Keep the build context small and free of secrets.
#
# Every service Dockerfile does COPY . . from the repo root, because the modules
# depend on pkg and pkg/node via go.work replace directives. Without this, .git,
# generated keys, and local databases are copied into the build context and
# potentially into an image layer.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Signing keys. These must never reach an image layer: an image is readable by
# anyone who can pull it, and a key in an image cannot be rotated without a
# rebuild. The auth node mounts its key from a Secret at runtime.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
jwt-keys/

# Local databases and build artifacts
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
auth.db
notification.db
*.test
*.out

# Documentation and local tooling that the build does not need
docs/
tests/
scripts/
.vscode/
.github/
*.md

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vs/